WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.750
Vsauce, Kevin here.

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:08.910
Imagine the horror of being arrested in connection
to a crime the entire world is reading about,

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:15.429
on the basis of irrefutable fingerprint evidence,
that you KNOW you didn’t commit.

00:00:15.429 --> 00:00:21.040
How do you defend yourself against a century
of science and math that just… aren’t

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.040
wrong?

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:27.900
And how can you possibly win when you’re
up against the FBI, and your own fingerprint

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.880
expert says your fingerprints are a match?

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.370
The first arrest of an American in connection
with the Madrid train bombings… what led

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.690
the FBI to Portland, Oregon?

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:50.399
Supporters of the man say agents are on the
wrong track.

00:00:50.399 --> 00:00:56.430
In Spain, they call it 11M.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:03.420
On March 11, 2004, just 3 days before Spain’s
general elections, explosions ripped through

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.500
trains in Madrid.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:10.510
193 people were killed and about 2,000 were
injured.

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:15.480
Europe hadn’t experienced an attack on that
scale in decades, and it came in the wake

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:20.610
of 9/11 and at the peak of the global war
on terror.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:25.450
Fingerprints were found on a bag that contained
detonating devices, and Spanish authorities

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:28.570
put them into the Interpol database.

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:35.420
The FBI in the United States found a match
to Latent Fingerprint 17, and in May, Brandon

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:41.480
Mayfield, a U.S. Army veteran and family law
attorney who frequently worked with low-income

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:44.890
clients in Portland, Oregon, took the blame.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:52.850
How does a lawyer 5,403 miles away from a
crime become its prime suspect?

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:59.850
To understand what went wrong here, we need
to go all the way back to Darwin.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:04.630
Throughout the 1800’s, scientists advanced
the notion that a pattern of epidermal ridges

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:10.909
on human fingertips, toes, and palms were
unique to each human, and they could be used

00:02:10.909 --> 00:02:16.629
as a proof of one’s identity -- like a built-in
biological signature.

00:02:16.629 --> 00:02:21.379
Scottish surgeon Henry Faulds proposed that
they could be cataloged and recorded with

00:02:21.379 --> 00:02:24.900
ink, and he asked Charles Darwin for help.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:31.120
Darwin was a bit too old to undertake a real
analysis, so he passed it onto his cousin

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:36.150
Francis Galton -- whose many accomplishments
included identifying the statistical regression

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:41.689
to the mean and inventing a physical board
to demonstrate it that we now see on game

00:02:41.689 --> 00:02:42.689
shows.

00:02:42.689 --> 00:02:47.760
The science around fingerprint identification
flourished, and by the beginning of the 20th

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:53.290
century, it had become one of the best ways
to pinpoint criminals -- and especially repeat

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:54.290
offenders.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:59.489
It replaced systems like branding skin, which
France outlawed in 1832.

00:02:59.489 --> 00:03:05.480
It was much more scientific than Alphonse
Bertillon’s anthropometric forensics, a

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:11.299
measurement of physical factors including
head length, head breadth, length of middle

00:03:11.299 --> 00:03:16.290
finger, length of the left foot, eye color
and hair color -- by assigning values for

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:21.420
each, Bertillon claimed each person would
have a unique combination of data.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:27.909
Except… it wasn’t all that unique, since
so many physical attributes correlate with

00:03:27.909 --> 00:03:28.909
one another.

00:03:28.909 --> 00:03:37.709
Like, most tall people also have long arms,
you don’t find many 5 foot 3 men with 7-foot

00:03:37.709 --> 00:03:38.709
wingspans.

00:03:38.709 --> 00:03:44.310
Fingerprints were much more accurate, and
Bertllon developed a system of 16 identifiable

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:47.849
markers that remained standard for over a
century.

00:03:47.849 --> 00:03:53.719
Starting in 1924, the US government began
compiling and cataloging fingerprints, and

00:03:53.719 --> 00:03:57.879
by 2004, they had about 200 million on file.

00:03:57.879 --> 00:04:03.599
A wavelet scalar quantization algorithm was
employed to compress the 500 pixel-per-inch

00:04:03.599 --> 00:04:11.010
images down to a file size of just 500kb -- which
meant easier storage, quicker access, and

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:14.230
smoother online transfers globally.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:15.540
Like to Spain.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:20.799
And by that time, it had been a century since
Francis Galton’s forgotten warning that,

00:04:20.799 --> 00:04:27.221
“A complex pattern [like fingerprints] is
capable of suggesting various readings, as

00:04:27.221 --> 00:04:32.500
the figuring on a wallpaper may suggest a
variety of forms and faces to those who have

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:35.490
such fancies.”

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:41.720
Even though the prints sent from Spain were
low quality, an FBI examiner signed an affidavit

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:51.160
stating that, “the FBI lab stands by their
conclusion of a 100 percent positive identification.”

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:57.949
In the weeks leading up to his arrest, Brandon
felt like he was being watched… because

00:04:57.949 --> 00:05:00.180
he was literally being watched.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:05.650
FBI documents show that as soon as Brandon’s
fingerprints popped as a potential match,

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:11.700
he was immediately under 24-hour FBI surveillance,
including phone and digital monitoring.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:18.810
He also suspected break-ins at his home and
his office, because… they were both really

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:20.050
broken into.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:23.419
They were convinced Mayfied was involved.

00:05:23.419 --> 00:05:24.810
Here’s a question!

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:30.440
If fingerprints are so foolproof, why was
an innocent man harassed by the government

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:36.180
and detained for weeks as he wondered why
they thought he was connected to a crime on

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:37.319
another continent?

00:05:37.319 --> 00:05:39.790
We’ll explore that in a second.

